  "reason": "RNA-only multiprofile avgpool is currently best, with scvi_n200 outperforming PCA and scGPT (0.650 vs 0.591/0.530 accuracy), and multiprofile helped PCA over singleprofile. The key uncertainty is whether scvi_n200 also requires multiprofile/aggregation or can perform well in a simpler singleprofile setting. config_004 tests scvi_n200 with singleprofile, isolating the profile effect for the best RNA encoder and comparing it to config_001 (singleprofile PCA) and config_005 (multiprofile scvi). This completes the central RNA encoder/profile factorial, avoids adding image/fusion changes, and is likely to clarify whether to keep a simpler singleprofile model before spending budget on more complex multimodal designs."
